On Wed, 28 Mar 2007 01:01:08 +0200, guns <sungmustpae@gmail.com> wrote:

> I'm actually slowly working on a patch based on the previously
> mentioned Enhanced Artifacts patch by Nephi. Many of the ideas
> presented by the OP are present in this patch (so much so that I
> suspect he's at least somewhat familiar with it), and are very good
> ideas.
>
> The very best idea, of course, is that all the various banes (ie all
> artifacts that target specific creatures) are made more useful by
> granting various intrinsics or properties that are generally useful,
> and especially useful (or plausibly useful) in fighting the targeted
> monster. So granting reflection to Dragonbane and hungerless
> regeneration to Trollbane offsets the uselessness of their narrow
> scope, as well as helping battle dragons and trolls. Nephi also gives
> them targeted warning (a la Sting) and +d20 instead of x2 damage,
> decreasing the need for enchanting the artifact or expending skill
> slots. (Nephi's patch does a bunch more; go check it out)

> Finally, I'd like to mention a couple more good ideas that I've ran
> across in case the OP is actually going to make a patch. L (http://
> www.greyfire.org/~l/nethack.html) has a couple of artifact patches
> that grant the Heart of Ahriman displacement ("It seems to be in two
> or more places at once, even though you are holding it.") and strength
> (like GoP) to the Sceptre of Might ("As you pick up the Sceptre of
> Might it seems heavy at first, but as you hold it strength flows into
> your arms."). In these cases, the game itself is offering a YANI.

